      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "To find the range of the function \\( G(x) = |x+1| - |x-1| \\), we need to consider three cases based on the values of \\( x \\) because the behavior of absolute values changes depending on whether \\( x \\) is in a positive, zero, or negative region with respect to \\(-1\\) and \\(1\\).\n\n1. **Case \\( x < -1 \\):**\n    - \\( x+1 < 0 \\)\n    - \\( x-1 < 0 \\)\n\nHence,\n\\[ |x+1| = -(x+1) = -x-1 \\]\n\\[ |x-1| = -(x-1) = -x+1 \\]\n\nCombining these,\n\\[\nG(x) = (-x-1) - (-x+1) = -x-1 + x-1 = -2\n\\]\n\n2. **Case \\( -1 \\le x < 1 \\):**\n    - \\( x+1 \\ge 0 \\)\n    - \\( x-1 < 0 \\)\n\nHence,\n\\[ |x+1| = x+1 \\]\n\\[ |x-1| = -(x-1) = -x+1 \\]\n\nCombining these,\n\\[\nG(x) = (x+1) - (-x+1) = x+1 + x-1 = 2x\n\\]\n\nIn this interval, \\( G(x) = 2x \\) will cover from \\( -2 \\) to \\( 2 \\) inclusive as \\( x \\) ranges from \\(-1\\) to \\( 1 \\).\n\n3. **Case \\( x \\ge 1 \\):**\n    - \\( x+1 \\ge 0 \\)\n    - \\( x-1 \\ge 0 \\)\n\nHence,\n\\[ |x+1| = x+1 \\]\n\\[ |x-1| = x-1 \\]\n\nCombining these,\n\\[\nG(x) = (x+1) - (x-1) = x+1-x+1 = 2\n\\]\n\nFinally, according to the ranges derived for each case, the overall \\( G(x) \\) function is within the interval \\([-2, 2]\\).\n\nHence, the range of the function is\n\\[\n\\boxed{[-2, 2]}\n\\]",
